---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro';

const originFixCode = `# Pass multiple comma-separated origins if running frontend & backend on different ports
npx copypatch serve --port 4040 --db ./copypatch.sqlite --origin "http://localhost:5173,https://my-website.com"`;

const passwordResetCode = `# Invalidate all active sessions and prompt for new passphrase
npx copypatch password --db ./copypatch.sqlite`;

const viteProxyCode = `// vite.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      '/__copypatch/api/v1': {
        target: 'http://localhost:4040',
        changeOrigin: true,
      },
    },
  },
});`;

const nextHydrationFixCode = `// app/page.tsx (Server Component)
import { NextCopyPatchProvider } from '@copypatch/next';
import { fetchServerSnapshot } from '@copypatch/next/server';

export default async function Page() {
  const snapshot = await fetchServerSnapshot('en');
  return (
    <NextCopyPatchProvider locale="en" initialSnapshot={snapshot}>
      {/* Page Content */}
    </NextCopyPatchProvider>
  );
}`;

const filePermissionsCode = `chmod 755 /data
chmod 644 /data/copypatch.sqlite*`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Troubleshooting & Diagnostics"
  description="Diagnostic guide and solutions for common CopyPatch issues, CORS errors, CSRF failures, and SSR hydration mismatches."
>
  <h1>Troubleshooting & Diagnostics</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    This guide lists common errors, diagnostic checklists, and resolution steps for both development and production environments.
  </p>

  <h2>Diagnostic Matrix</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Error Code / Symptom</th>
        <th>Root Cause</th>
        <th>Resolution</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>ORIGIN_REJECTED (403)</code></td>
        <td>Client Origin header does not match configured <code>--origin</code> allowlist.</td>
        <td>Add the client URL to the server CLI <code>--origin</code> argument.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>CSRF_FAILED (403)</code></td>
        <td>Missing or mismatched <code>x-copypatch-csrf</code> request header.</td>
        <td>Ensure edit session is active and cookies are not blocked by browser extensions.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>REVISION_CONFLICT (409)</code></td>
        <td>Another user published or saved draft changes concurrently.</td>
        <td>Refresh snapshot to view latest changes before reapplying local edits.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>SQLITE_BUSY (500)</code></td>
        <td>Database file locked or filesystem lacks directory write permissions.</td>
        <td>Ensure database is in WAL mode and parent directory has read-write permissions.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Edit toolbar missing</strong></td>
        <td><code>?copypatch=1</code> missing from URL or provider not mounted.</td>
        <td>Confirm <code>CopyPatchProvider</code> wraps the active component tree.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Next.js Hydration Warning</strong></td>
        <td>Server rendered fallback text but client fetched different copy.</td>
        <td>Use <code>fetchServerSnapshot()</code> in Server Component before rendering.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>1. Edit Mode (?copypatch=1) Does Not Activate</h2>
  <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Navigating to <code>?copypatch=1</code> shows the standard visitor website without the floating toolbar or passphrase prompt.</p>
  <p><strong>Diagnostic Checklist:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Verify that your root layout or view component is wrapped with <code>&lt;CopyPatchProvider&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li>Ensure the search parameter is exact (case-sensitive): <code>?copypatch=1</code>.</li>
    <li>Check your browser developer console for any script errors or bundle loading failures.</li>
    <li>If using React 19 / Vite, verify that dynamic <code>import()</code> is allowed by your Content Security Policy (CSP).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. CORS or Origin Rejection (403 ORIGIN_REJECTED)</h2>
  <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Saving copy changes fails with <code>403 Forbidden: ORIGIN_REJECTED</code>.</p>
  <p><strong>Cause:</strong> CopyPatch enforces strict origin checks to prevent unauthorized cross-site mutations.</p>
  <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Specify all allowed client URLs to the server CLI:</p>

  <CodeBlock code={originFixCode} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />

  <p>
    Alternatively, proxy API requests through your Vite dev server to keep frontend and API on the same origin:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code={viteProxyCode} lang="ts" title="vite.config.ts" />

  <h2>3. Passphrase Lost or Session Invalidation</h2>
  <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> You forgot the configured passphrase or need to revoke all currently active editor sessions immediately.</p>
  <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Run the interactive password command against your database:</p>

  <CodeBlock code={passwordResetCode} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />

  <p>
    This atomically updates the Argon2id hash in <code>auth_credentials</code> and wipes all active rows in the <code>sessions</code> table, instantly logging out all browser sessions.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Next.js SSR Hydration Mismatch</h2>
  <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Browser console logs <code>Warning: Text content did not match. Server: "..." Client: "..."</code>.</p>
  <p><strong>Cause:</strong> The Server Component rendered with hardcoded React fallback copy, but the client hydrated with published copy from CopyPatch storage.</p>
  <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Fetch the snapshot on the server during SSR and pass it via <code>initialSnapshot</code>:</p>

  <CodeBlock code={nextHydrationFixCode} lang="tsx" title="app/page.tsx" />

  <h2>5. SQLite File Permissions & WAL Mode</h2>
  <p><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Backend logs <code>SQLITE_CANTOPEN</code> or <code>SQLITE_READONLY</code>.</p>
  <p><strong>Cause:</strong> SQLite needs write permissions to both the database file itself and the parent directory to create <code>copypatch.sqlite-wal</code> and <code>copypatch.sqlite-shm</code> files.</p>
  <p><strong>Fix:</strong> Grant read-write permissions to the executing user or Docker container:</p>

  <CodeBlock code={filePermissionsCode} lang="bash" title="Terminal" />
</DocsLayout>
